  "student_passage": "Our group was making a model shelf for the school reading corner. I had drawn the plan and felt very (1) ____ about it. When Mina asked me to check the numbers again, I thought she was simply (2) ____ the work. We had only one afternoon left, and I wanted to start cutting.\n\nMina did not argue. She put two thick pieces of card on the table and placed the long piece between them. It would not (3) ____. I had measured the outside width of the model but had forgotten that the two side panels would take up some of the (4) ____.\n\nFor a moment, I tried to (5) ____ my drawing. Then I saw the model in front of me and stopped making excuses. Mina was not questioning how hard I had worked; she was checking whether the parts would go together. We (6) ____ the width before using any wood. That small change saved material we could not replace with our limited budget.\n\nI offered Mina the pencil and asked her to add her measurements to mine. The final plan was a (7) ____ effort, with notes in two different styles of handwriting. Before making the real shelf, we built a second model to (8) ____ it. This time, every part fitted.\n\nWhen classmates praised the finished shelf, I (9) ____ Mina's early question instead of taking all the credit. I now try to see a careful question as a (10) ____ to improve a plan, even when the plan is my own.",
